+  // The state array is fixed (Sleigh::DisassemblyCache sizes it at 75,
+  // sleigh.cc:457). Bytes that are not an instruction can drive the
+  // constructor walk past that, and indexing past the end corrupted memory:
+  // an ARM image decoded in Thumb mode at a data address took the console
+  // down with it. Out of states means what the caller already handles -- no
+  // instruction here.
+  if (alloc >= (int4)state.size())
